# CompTIA A+ Core 1 (220-1201) — Mobile Accessories & Connectivity Cheat Sheet

## 1. USB

| Version       | Year        | Max Speed  | Notes                                   |
|---------------|-------------|------------|-----------------------------------------|
| USB 1.0       | 1996        | 12 Mbps    | Basic peripherals (keyboard/mouse)      |
| USB 2.0       | ~2000       | 480 Mbps   | Introduced USB hubs                     |
| USB 3.0       | 2008        | 5 Gbps     | Better power efficiency                 |
| USB 3.1 / 3.2 | 2013 / 2017 | 10–20 Gbps | Improved encoding                       |
| USB4          | 2019        | 40 Gbps    | Unified standard, Thunderbolt 3 support |
| USB4 v2.0     | 2022        | 80 Gbps    | Current standard                        |

**Connector types:** USB-A (standard rectangular), USB-B (square, printers/scanners), Mini/Micro-USB (older mobiles/cameras), USB-C (reversible, data+power+display).

**Power Delivery:** USB PD 3.1 supports up to **240 W**, with intelligent negotiation between devices. "Smart charging" often stops at ~80–85% instead of 100%.

**USB-C vs. Thunderbolt:** Same physical connector/port, fully interchangeable. Only visual difference = the small lightning-bolt icon on Thunderbolt cables. TB3/TB4 = up to 40 Gbps; USB4 v2.0 over Thunderbolt = up to 80 Gbps.

