## 2. Lightning Connector

- Apple-proprietary, 8-pin, fully reversible (no "top/bottom").
- Found on older iPhones/iPads (pre USB-C switch); newer Apple devices use USB-C.
- **MFi certification** ("Made for iPhone/iPad") ensures full compatibility/performance — non-MFi cables may throw accessory errors.
- Roughly matches USB 2.0 speeds.
- **Troubleshooting:** clean port with compressed air/ESD-safe brush, use MFi cables, keep OS updated.

---

## 3. Serial Connections

Transmits data **1 bit at a time** (vs. 8 bits/parallel) — simple, reliable, used in legacy/industrial/embedded systems, POS systems, networking config ports, medical devices.

| Standard | Speed           | Range                    | Connector        | Use case                                             |
|----------|-----------------|--------------------------|------------------|------------------------------------------------------|
| RS-232   | 300–115,200 bps | ~50 ft                   | DB-9 / DB-25     | Legacy PCs, modems, printers                         |
| RS-422   | up to 10 Mbps   | up to 4,000 ft (1,200 m) | —                | Point-to-point, industrial automation, telecom       |
| RS-485   | (like RS-422)   | (like RS-422)            | —                | Multi-point bus, **SCADA**, HVAC, factory automation |

- **Baud rate ≠ bit rate** unless purely digital (1 state change = 1 bit).
- **USB-to-serial adapters** (incl. **FTDI** chipsets) bridge modern devices to legacy serial gear.
- Modern alternatives: Ethernet, **CAN bus** (vehicle systems).

