## 4. Bluetooth Pairing

**Pairing process:** enable Bluetooth on both devices → set accessory to pairing mode → select device from list → confirm (PIN if required) → link key stored for future auto-reconnect.

**Common issues:** device not found, repeated disconnects, PIN mismatch, interference (shares 2.4/5 GHz band with Wi-Fi).
**Fixes:** restart devices, stay in range, clear paired-device history, reduce Wi-Fi interference.

**Security risks:**
- *Bluejacking* – unsolicited messages
- *Bluesnarfing* – unauthorized data access
- *Man-in-the-middle* – intercepted communication

**Best practices:** disable Bluetooth when idle, use **Secure Simple Pairing (SSP)** (link-key based, no PIN), clear old pairings, keep firmware updated.

| Version | Range          | Speed  | Notes                                                      |
|---------|----------------|--------|------------------------------------------------------------|
| 4.0     | ~10 m (30 ft)  | 1 Mbps | Basic security                                             |
| 5.0     | ~40 m (130 ft) | 2 Mbps | Improved encryption/efficiency                             |
| 5.4     | ~60 m (200 ft) | 2 Mbps | Low Energy Audio, periodic advertising, strongest security |

