## 5. NFC vs. Bluetooth vs. Wi-Fi Hotspot

**NFC:** 13.56 MHz, range ≤ 4 cm, speeds 106/212/424 kbps. Three modes: **peer-to-peer**, **reader/writer** (reads/writes NFC tags), **card emulation** (mobile payments).

| Feature     | NFC                    | Bluetooth           | Wi-Fi                  |
|-------------|------------------------|---------------------|------------------------|
| Range       | ≤4 cm                  | 10–100 m            | 30–300 m               |
| Speed       | 106–424 kbps           | 1–3 Mbps            | 100+ Mbps              |
| Pairing     | Instant tap            | Pairing process     | Network authentication |
| Power use   | Very low               | Moderate            | High                   |
| Typical use | Payments, access, tags | Audio, file sharing | Internet access        |

**NFC security risks:** eavesdropping, data corruption, relay attacks.
**Mitigations:** enable secure NFC mode, use tokenization for payments, keep NFC apps/firmware updated.

